Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["UniversalTime", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"0913c0fb-d132-4f17-b990-f09af2e131f9"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["UniversalTime"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/UniversalTime", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10dad207-07a9-41cc-a412-94bf5ec3e30a"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the height of every event of the directed acyclic graph ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ": the number of edges of a longest chain from a source to it, zero exactly \
on the sources.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"aa00d97f-2868-4685-932a-5099545e1097"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: the universal time of an event ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = max over the sources ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " below ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of \[Tau](",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "), the number of edges of a longest chain from ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "; on a source ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " = 0. Equivalently ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = 1 + max ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ") over the direct predecessors ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", which is how it is computed, in one pass over a topological order."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b6a69765-acd2-4f79-88b5-e8033985161b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A time function on a causal graph is an integer function that increases \
along every edge. The universal time is the least one that is nonnegative: \
any other such function ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " satisfies ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \[GreaterEqual] ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "), by induction along a longest chain. It needs no observer and no choice; \
its level sets are the slices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSlice"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraSlice", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "38a84b1e-8766-49c8-ae91-41f893ac6220"],
 " of the universal foliation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["UniversalFoliation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/UniversalFoliation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d3ddff87-403c-44ac-85af-1913b0f657f1"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e884d912-f041-4179-99d1-f5443369662b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is an association ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " \[RightArrow] ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") over the events of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ", in the order of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"VertexList", "[", "g", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b151f6f4-dfa0-429a-a563-fd73b2334231"],
 ". It is a density in the sense of InfraGeometry: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateHighlight", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7e209139-6b27-468d-bdb2-bbced854ec7f"],
 " draws it, a source with value 0 left plain."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5f4c6d6f-5eab-4b9d-ba94-6a016cfc9b4d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The longest chain from a source is the discrete proper time of the observer \
that started at the beginning: on a geodesic observer from a source, the \
universal time of the ",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 "-th tick is ",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] 1. On the diamond lattice the universal time of (",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 ") is ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 ", twice the coordinate time; on the cylinder lattice it is the row."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"40ab7c86-4565-42e5-ac7d-84f53cab3c2e"],

Cell["Corresponding notions:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"50491258-0926-41a1-b905-06da04753bae"],

